ay Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332819/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-31T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Wizards & Workouts - FREE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/events/316670381/","description":"Do you consider rolling dice strength training?\nCan you run a D&D campaign, but not a city block?\nIf so, **WIZARDS & WORKOUTS** is for you.\n\nMy name is Peter Reynolds. I'm a writer and lover of role playing games. I'm also out of shape. I've been looking for ways to motivate myself to start working out with the same enthusiasm I bring to my Dungeons & Dragons campaign.\n\nThe plan is simple: host a fun, live role playing game where players take on the role of their favourite fantasy characters. The catch? You need to exercise if you want to succeed. Fighting a dragon? A fireball might cost you 5 pushups. Crossing a rooftop? Can you balance on one foot for a minute?\n\nBy combining simple, low impact exercises, including walking & stretching, with an interactive adventure, we'll all get healthier, have fun and maybe meet some new friends along the way. All fitness levels are welcome (as are dogs), and no previous knowledge of Dungeons & Dragons is necessary.\n\nWe meet in front of Broadview subway station at 10:00 am sharp and then walk to the Outdoor Fitness Station in Riverdale Park East (there are washrooms). At noon we start walking west, through the park, ending at the Blake House Restaurant \\* (Wellesley & Jarvis) by 12:30.\n\nAll sessions are free and I’ll be running them till it gets too cold. Hope to see you there!\n\n* The Blake House is where our Sci-Fi and Fantasy Writers' Group meets every Saturday from 1pm - 4pm to critique each other’s work. For more information on this event. Check out our Meetup events page.","startDate":"2026-10-31T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Broadview Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Ontario","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"769 Broadview Avenue, Ontario, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Serving at Daily Bread Food Bank, Halloween morning 🎃","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-joy/events/316785581/","description":"Hi everyone 🙏\n\nWe'll be serving together at Daily Bread Food Bank in Etobicoke on Halloween morning. They can take 8 of us, so register early to save your spot.\n\nMore than 1 in 10 people in Toronto now rely on food banks... visits are at an all-time high.\n\n**We'll start with a short tour, then help sort and pack donated food, or wherever they need us that morning. No experience needed, and it's** **free to join**.\n\n✦ **Saturday, October 31, 10am to 12pm** (please come 5 to 10 min early)\n✦ 191 New Toronto Street, Etobicoke (Lake Shore Blvd W & Islington)\n✦ Free parking, or the 110C bus from Islington Station\n✦ **Closed-toe shoes please**\n✦ Ages 18+\n\n**How to join**\n\n1. Create your Toronto Joy account. It's one time only and takes about 3 minutes.\n\n[https://torontojoy.org/register/](https://torontojoy.org/register/)\n\n2. Register on the event page by **Friday, October 16**:\n\nhttps://torontojoy.org/event/volunteer-at-daily-bread-food-bank/\n\nAlready have an account? Skip to step 2.\n\nOnly people registered on our website can take a spot.\n\nOnce you're registered, I'll send you Daily Bread's waiver to sign and our WhatsApp group link for day-of updates.\n\nIf you sign up, please do so with the intention of attending... Daily Bread is counting on us.\n\nWould be great to serve together! ❤️\nAmar and Team","startDate":"2026-10-31T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"191 New Toronto St","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"191 New Toronto St, Etobicoke, ON M8V 2E7, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Joy","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-joy/"},"performer":"Toronto Joy"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎃🍂 Halloween Day: The Fall Colours of High Park & Ghost Stories 👻","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316183452/","description":"# 🎃🍂 Halloween Day: The Fall Colours of High Park & Ghost Stories 👻\n\n### Fall Colours, Spooky Stories & A Little Halloween Fun\n\nIt's Halloween — so why should the ghosts get to have all the fun at night?\n\nJoin us for a **Halloween Day walk through High Park**, where we'll enjoy the fall colours while stopping along the way for some of the park's stranger, spookier, and downright weird stories.\nHigh Park has a long history of ghost stories and local legends.\n\nFrom stories connected to the **War of 1812** — yes, *that* War of 1812 — to tales of mysterious deaths and people who may not have completely left the park behind, there's plenty of history to make an ordinary fall walk a little more interesting.\nBut don't worry.\n\n**This isn't a terrifying ghost hunt.**\n\nIt's Halloween in the middle of the day. 👻☀️\nThink **fall colours, creepy stories, a few laughs, and just enough spooky atmosphere to make you look over your shoulder once or twice.**\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll walk through **High Park**, stopping at different locations along the way while I share stories connected to the park's history and ghostly legends.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Enjoy the fall colours 🍂\n* Explore some of High Park's most interesting locations\n* Hear stories of ghosts, legends, and strange events 👻\n* Learn a little about the park's history\n* Take photos and enjoy the scenery 📸\n* Have some Halloween fun along the way 🎃\n\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace, with regular stops for storytelling.\nThe walk will remain **outside throughout** — there is no entry into buildings.\n\n***\n\n## 🎃 Halloween Day — So Let's Have Some Fun\n\nThis isn't meant to be a serious paranormal investigation.\nIt's a **Halloween walk**.\n\nSome stories are creepy. Some are strange. Some might make you wonder whether there's actually something going on.\nAnd some are just a good excuse to tell a spooky story while walking through the fall leaves.\n\n**You don't have to believe in ghosts.**\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nHigh Park can be cool and damp in late October, so bring a warm jacket and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll be walking at a steady pace, with stops along the way for stories and photos.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park sign on the west side at Bloor Street West & High Park Avenue\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶 **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** Back where we started\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated, guided storytelling experience**, rather than one of our regular group walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Warm fall jacket or layers\n📸 Camera or phone\n🎃 Halloween spirit\nAnd if you want to wear a costume...\n**I'm certainly not going to stop you.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* People who love Halloween 🎃\n* Anyone who enjoys ghost stories\n* Fall-colour enthusiasts 🍂\n* History buffs\n* People looking for something different to do on Halloween Day\n* Anyone who enjoys a good story and a few laughs\n* People who want to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the fall colours.** 🍂\n**Stay for the ghost stories.** 👻\n**Leave with a new connection — if the ghosts don't get you first.** 🎃","startDate":"2026-10-31T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"High Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Bloor and High Park Avenue, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/"},"performer":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Saturday Salsa Matinee | Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/salsa-bachata-kizomba-gta/events/316744644/","description":"Best way to get a hold of us is on our [WhatsApp chat](https://chat.whatsapp.com/KpFOsXEuXRWB7uOYorJNPU), also great way to join a community of amazing like-minded people :)\n\nAdmission includes:\n1-Hour Salsa Lesson\nSocial Dancing - DJ Geronimo's top Salsa, Bachata & Cha cha Latin hits.\n\nIt's an excellent opportunity to practice and improve your dance to the tunes of world Salsa music by DJ Geronimo and guest DJs. Have a favourite song ? We're also accepting music requests\nAtmosphere: Friendly and Laid back.\n\nDancers of all levels are welcome for social (No partner required)\nDoor: $10\n\nFREE LESSON (with admission to social dancing) 2pm\n\nSOCIAL DANCING 3-6pm\n\\*Please check calendar as in some rare occasions time changes slightly\n\nVenue: Tempo Dance Collective – 1610a Bloor St W, Toronto\n\nEveryone is welcome!\nJoin our WhatsApp group:\n[https://chat.whatsapp.com/Kj63TzHIqYL5hPrRJolhyD](https://chat.whatsapp.com/KpFOsXEuXRWB7uOYorJNPU)\n\nHosts:\n\nMaya & Gary\nCanada SBK (Formerly TSF)","startDate":"2026-10-31T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tempo Dance Collective","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1610A Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M6P 1A7, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Salsa | Bachata | Kizomba GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/salsa-bachata-kizomba-gta/"},"performer":"Salsa | Bachata | Kizomba GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Learn To Carve: Labour Day Workshop","url":"https://www.meetup.com/craft-hub-toronto/events/316688979/","description":"Join us on Halloween from 2:00-5:00 to learn how to hand carve your own spooky wooden firgurine! No experience is needed and all materials are provided. Bring a friend to get a 20$ discount and enjoy a spookily fun time! Register through this link: [https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/learn-to-carve-workshop-halloween ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/learn-to-carve-workshop-halloween)","startDate":"2026-10-31T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"GlobalDWS","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2, 68 Railside Rd, North York, ON M3A 1A3, Canada, toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Craft Hub Toronto: Woodcarving Workshops","url":"https://www.meetup.com/craft-hub-toronto/"},"performer":"Craft Hub Toronto: Woodcarving Workshops"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Contemporary dance - weekly class | Beginner Friendly | Toronto North","url":"https://www.meetup.com/contemporary-dance-kw/events/316426444/","description":"Instagram @nina.philflow\n\nA contemporary dance class for anyone who wants to explore movement — no experience needed, just an open mind and comfortable clothes.\nEach session may include a mix of:\n\n* Movement fundamentals and body awareness\n* Improvisation and play\n* Short choreographic phrases\n* Simple partnering and group dynamics\n\nWe work with ideas like weight, flow, momentum, and sensing — building a physical vocabulary that's accessible whether you've never danced before or come from another movement background.\n**Where:** 155 East Beaver Creek Rd, Richmond Hill\n**When:** Every Saturday 2:30-4:00pm\n**Cost:** $25 for 1st session \\| $45 drop\\-in \\| $40 come with a friend or 4\\-class pack \\| $35 for 8\\-class pack\n\n**About the Instructor**\nNina holds an MA in Dance Performance from Trinity Laban, London (UK), and has taught in London, Toronto, Waterloo and Hong Kong. She brings a warm, exploratory approach to every class and believes dance is for everyone.\n\n**What to Bring**\n\n* Comfortable clothes you can move freely in (long pants recommended)\n* Socks — avoid very slippery ones\n* A bottle of water\n\nLooking forward to dancing together — feel free to reach out if you have any questions.\n\nFor dance tips, class snippets, and book recommendations, follow along on Instagram **@nina.philflow**\n\nlink for sign-up and more info:\nhttps://forms.gle/dbtx7awqKRqdT45t5","startDate":"2026-10-31T18:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Sunling School of Dance","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Richmond Hill","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"155 East Beaver Creek Road Unit 1, Richmond Hill, Richmond Hill, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Contemporary dance KW and Toronto North","url":"https://www.meetup.com/contemporary-dance-kw/"},"performer":"Contemporary dance KW and Toronto North"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"On bavarde","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/events/316616447/","description":"RENCONTRE EN PRÉSENTIEL AU NORTH YORK CENTRE\n\nRejoignez-nous pour deux heures de conversation en français en personne.\n\nOÙ : North York Centre, Food Court\n(5150 rue Yonge, le batiment immediatement au nord du square Mel Lastman, métro North York)\n\nQUAND : samedi de 16h00 (4 pm) à 18h00\n\nA bientôt!","startDate":"2026-10-31T20:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"North York City Centre (same bldg as the NY Library), Food court","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5150 Yonge Street (WEST side!!!), next to Mel Lastman Sq., North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"North York French Language Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/"},"performer":"North York French Language Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎃  Halloween Dinner @ The Haunted Keg Mansion 👻","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316545787/","description":"# 🎃 **Halloween Dinner @ The Haunted Keg Mansion 👻**\n\nThis year marks our **14th annual Halloween Dinner at The Keg Mansion** — a tradition I started with this group fourteen years ago.\n\n⚠️ **This event fills up every year, and spots are limited to just 30 people. If you want to join us, please make sure you’re committed before signing up.**\n\nIf you don’t already know, The Keg Mansion is one of the most haunted buildings in Toronto. Some guests claim to have seen the Lady in the window upstairs, and the women’s washroom is famous for its ghostly encounters. We may not know exactly where we’ll be seated, but the second floor is known to be especially active… if you dare. 👻\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ The Keg Mansion\n\nThe Keg is a classic steakhouse with a wide range of dishes and price points, so there’s something for everyone. Whether you’re coming for the meal, the company, or the possibility of encountering something from the other side, you’ll be part of one of our longest-running Halloween traditions.\n\n📋 **Menu:**[ Click Here](https://thekeg.com/en/locations/mansion/menu)\n💲 **Cost of Meal:** $$$\n\n***\n\n## 👥 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Spot:** I’ll be waiting outside The Keg Mansion wearing my Moose Hat. Please don’t go inside without me.\n🕖 **Meetup Time:** 6:45 pm\n\n**I’ll only wait 5 minutes!**\n\n***\n\n## 🎭 Dress Code & Church Street\n\nEvery year people ask if they can dress up — the answer is **YES!** Costumes are welcome. 🎃\nAfter dinner, anyone who wants to head to **Church Street for Toronto’s famous Halloween Festival** is welcome to go.\n\nIt gets **very crowded**, so I won’t be joining the group or leading everyone through the festival. I’ll help anyone who wants to go together find one another, point you in the right direction, and make sure you know where you’re headed.\nFrom there, you’re on your own to enjoy the madness! 👻\n\n***\n\n## 💵 SAVE YOUR SPOT — PLEASE READ BEFORE RSVPing\n\n**Spots are limited to 24 people.**\n\nTo secure your spot, a **$25 e-transfer must be sent to [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com) within 24 hours of signing up.**\nThis applies to **everyone**.\n\nIt does not matter whether you joined the group yesterday, have been here for fourteen years, or have been a member in good standing for years. **If you are attending this event, you pay the $25 save-your-spot fee. There are no exceptions.**\n\nHere’s how it works:\n\n* **$25 must be paid within 24 hours of signing up.**\n* **$20 will be returned to you when you show up.**\n* **$5 is the Meetup fee that supports the group.**\n* If payment is not received within 24 hours, **your spot may be given to someone else.**\n* **There are no refunds for any reason.**\n\nPlease do not sign up unless you are **100% committed to attending**. With only 30 spots available, every spot matters.\nI’m not going to chase people for payment. If you sign up, you are responsible for sending the $25 within the 24-hour deadline.\n\n⚠️ **Waiting List:** If the event is full and you are placed on the waiting list, **do not send the $25 e-transfer.** Only send payment if I contact you and confirm that a spot has become available. Your spot is not confirmed until I have contacted you and confirmed it.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n* Sometimes things happen and I may need to cancel — please watch for updates.\n* Please **don’t call the restaurant** — they won’t know anything about this event. Direct all questions to me.\n* This group is open to everyone: singles, couples, and anyone looking to be social, make friends, and have fun. We also host movies, walks, hikes, arts & culture outings, and more!\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew.** For questions, post on the wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**","startDate":"2026-10-31T22:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"THE KEG MANSION","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"515 Jarvis Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Halloween Dance Party and Scavenger Hunt","url":"https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/events/316341733/","description":"**It's a Halloween Dance Party and Scavenger Hunt!**\n\n**Location: Party Room 51 Trolley Crescent**\n**(Scavenger Hunt is under the bridge)**\n\n**Fee:**\n**$20 by October 19th******\n**$25 from October 20th to 28th**\n**Send to**\n**boots4hikingthsix@gmail.com**\n\n**Party Details**\n***Theme**: Unmask your hidden self.*\n*** Vibe*: Grown-up drinks, killer costumes, and zero filters.\n\n**Drop the mask and let your true monster out to play this Halloween.**\nPrize for best costume!\nEvery day we wear the mask of the professional, the polite, and the responsible. Not tonight. This Halloween, it’s time to shed your civilized skin and unleash your **real personality**—no filters, no judgements, just pure, unadulterated fun.\nCome as who you *actually* are on the inside.\n🖤 The Ritual\n\n*** Date: **Saturday, October 31st, 2026\n*** Time: **7:00 PM until the spirits fade**\n*** Lair: We are just confirming the venue. We will keep you posted!\n\n🍷 The Elements\n\n*** Potions & Brews: **Drinks and nibbles provided!\n*** Attire: **Costumes required. Dress as your inner alter-ego, your deepest obsession, or the version of you that only comes out after dark.\n*** The Vibe: **Dark beats, heavy pours, and wicked company.\nADMISSION IS $20,\n\nAre you brave enough to show your true colours?","startDate":"2026-10-31T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"51 Trolley Crescent","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"51 Trolley Cres, Toronto, ON M5A 0E9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"These Boots Are Made for Hiking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/"},"performer":"These Boots Are Made for Hiking"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎃 Halloween Special: Meet New People | + 50+ Board Games | 21–45","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/events/316791549/","description":"🎃 Looking for a fun way to meet new people in Toronto this Halloween?\n\nYou could walk into a room full of strangers and hope a conversation happens… or you could let us make the first step easy.\n\nJoin us for a Halloween Special at Stout Irish Pub, where Fast Friends takes the guesswork out of making new connections.\n\nThrough relaxed, professionally hosted conversations, rotations and Halloween-themed connection rounds, you'll meet 20+ people, discover common interests and have plenty of reasons to laugh and chat along the way.\n\n🎃 Costumes are welcome but completely optional — come dressed up, add a little Halloween flair, or simply come as you are.\n\nAnd the best part? The evening doesn't stop when the hosted rounds do.\nAfterwards, stick around at Stout for 50+ board games, drinks and more time to socialise with the people you've just met. 🎲🍻\n\nBook Early & Save: [https://toronto31stoct.eventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto31stoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\nEarly Bird: CAD $10 \\| Regular: CAD $15 \\| Door: CAD $20 cash\n\nAdvance tickets help us plan the right space and group size and ensure a well-organised experience for everyone.\n\n🤝 What to Expect\n7:00 PM — Welcome & Drinks\nMeet your host, Kruttika, grab a drink and settle in.\nComing alone? You're in good company. Many of our guests arrive solo, and our host will help you get comfortable, make introductions and get the evening started.\n\n7:30–8:30 PM — Hosted Fast Friends\nThis is where the evening really gets going.\nYou'll have a series of short, guided conversations, moving around the group so you get the chance to meet a variety of people rather than spending the whole evening talking to just one person.\nNo need to walk up to strangers and figure out what to say — we've created the structure for you.\n\n🎃 Halloween-Themed Connection Rounds\nAlongside the regular Fast Friends conversations, we'll add some Halloween-inspired themed rounds with fun prompts and challenges designed to get people laughing, talking and discovering what they have in common.\nExpect a few seasonal twists — nothing complicated, just an easy way to make the conversations even more fun.\n\n🎲 8:30 PM onwards — 50+ Board Games & Socialising\nDon't feel like heading home after the hosted rounds?\nStay and keep the evening going at Stout.\nWith 50+ board games available, you can join a game with people you've met, grab another drink, continue a conversation or simply mingle and see where the evening takes you.\nYou don't need to be a serious gamer — the games are simply another easy way to keep people interacting.\n\n🍻 And if you're staying later, Stout's After Dark Special runs from 9–11 PM, with $7 beers and $7 highballs, among other specials.\n\n❤️ Why This Event?\n✔️ Halloween Special 🎃\n✔️ Meet 25+ new people in one evening\n✔️ Professionally hosted conversations and rotations\n✔️ Halloween-themed connection rounds\n✔️ Costumes welcome — but completely optional\n✔️ 50+ board games at Stout 🎲\n✔️ Reserved area for our group\n✔️ Easy-to-reach Toronto location\n✔️ Relaxed Irish-pub atmosphere\n✔️ Most guests attend solo\n✔️ Meet members from across our Toronto social communities\n✔️ Ages 25–45\n✔️ Friendship-focused — not a dating event\n\n👥 Who Should Come?\nWhether you've recently moved to Toronto, have lived here for years, work from home and want a bigger social circle, or simply feel like meeting some different people — you're welcome.\nYou don't need to know anyone beforehand.\nCome by yourself, bring a friend, wear a costume or don't — the evening is designed to make it easy to get involved and start connecting.\n\n💳 Why Book in Advance?\nYour ticket helps us plan the right space, manage the group size and create a comfortable experience for everyone.\nOnline tickets are also cheaper than paying at the door.\n\n🌍 About Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years, Fast Friends has been helping people make genuine connections through professionally hosted social events in 30+ cities around the world.\nOur goal is simple: make meeting new people easier, more relaxed and more enjoyable.\nCome solo. We’ll guide the experience. You make the connections. ❤️","startDate":"2026-10-31T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus